WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.317 --> 00:00:02.173
- This is my ASMR video.

00:00:02.173 --> 00:00:03.516
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:03.516 --> 00:00:06.683
(mellow, jazzy music)

00:00:08.379 --> 00:00:13.203
- Today we're gonna be trying
some Japanese drunk snacks.

00:00:13.203 --> 00:00:14.905
Ooh, it's in a box.

00:00:14.905 --> 00:00:17.026
"Otsumami Set," that's cute.

00:00:17.026 --> 00:00:18.822
Also, it says "let's party" on it

00:00:18.822 --> 00:00:23.187
which is a directive I
much appreciate getting.

00:00:23.187 --> 00:00:24.167
- Woo!

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:25.676
Alright, okay.

00:00:25.676 --> 00:00:27.394
You know, I can trust anything

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:28.699
that's in a package like this.

00:00:28.699 --> 00:00:29.964
- [Both] Wasabi!

00:00:29.964 --> 00:00:31.272
- [Jen] Wow, these'll be good.

00:00:31.272 --> 00:00:33.221
- Okay, I'm excited now.

00:00:33.221 --> 00:00:34.894
- Yeah, we love wasabi-flavored things.

00:00:34.894 --> 00:00:36.282
- What did the A say to B?

00:00:36.282 --> 00:00:37.699
- What did it say?

00:00:37.699 --> 00:00:39.029
- Was-a-bi.

00:00:39.029 --> 00:00:40.195
- What does that mean?

00:00:40.195 --> 00:00:41.069
- It's a joke.

00:00:41.069 --> 00:00:42.352
- Oh. (laughs dramatically)

00:00:42.352 --> 00:00:43.260
- Oooh.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:44.362
- Is this like crackers?

00:00:44.362 --> 00:00:45.620
- You know when you said wasabi flavor

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.423
I thought I was gonna be
like I was eating wasabi.

00:00:47.423 --> 00:00:49.832
- It tastes kind of like a
Pop Chip with just like a hint

00:00:49.832 --> 00:00:52.215
of the wasabi nose-clearing flavor.

00:00:52.215 --> 00:00:53.474
- I like that cruch though.

00:00:53.474 --> 00:00:55.883
It's a really satisfying
crunch, are you ready for this?

00:00:55.883 --> 00:00:57.663
ASMR. (crunches loudly)

00:00:57.663 --> 00:00:59.000
- [Steven] Scallop, baby!

00:00:59.000 --> 00:00:59.833
(Jen chuckles)

00:00:59.833 --> 00:01:01.208
You all, scallops are good.

00:01:01.208 --> 00:01:03.382
- So, scallop flavored,
it smells pretty similar

00:01:03.382 --> 00:01:04.691
to the wasabi one.

00:01:04.691 --> 00:01:06.286
- I feel like I'm eating a bad version

00:01:06.286 --> 00:01:08.208
of a crostini with tuna.

00:01:08.208 --> 00:01:09.802
- I feel that way too, but I like it.

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:11.343
- Yeah, but you like everything.

00:01:11.343 --> 00:01:13.021
- So, let's just take a look at this.

00:01:13.021 --> 00:01:15.521
This is called "Gratz," oh "Cratz."

00:01:15.521 --> 00:01:16.667
- Crackers.
- I don't know how to read.

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:18.747
Cratz, so I guess they're crackers.

00:01:18.747 --> 00:01:22.387
They look like tiny little
Corn Nuts, honestly.

00:01:22.387 --> 00:01:24.636
This smells like hot dogs.
- Yeah.

00:01:24.636 --> 00:01:26.608
- These smell exactly like hot dogs.

00:01:26.608 --> 00:01:28.042
I hope they taste like hot dogs.

00:01:28.042 --> 00:01:28.982
And I got a nut?

00:01:28.982 --> 00:01:30.532
Okay, let's do it.

00:01:30.532 --> 00:01:31.449
Whoa.
- Yo.

00:01:32.348 --> 00:01:34.531
- These taste exactly like hot dogs!

00:01:34.531 --> 00:01:36.120
- I would buy this every day.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:37.711
- Okay, this one is
butter and salt flavored.

00:01:37.711 --> 00:01:39.291
- I'm gonna love this, I already know.

00:01:39.291 --> 00:01:43.029
- Wow, this smells like movie
theater buttered popcorn.

00:01:43.029 --> 00:01:45.386
- You know when they serve
you bread before a meal?

00:01:45.386 --> 00:01:46.242
- Mm-hmm.

00:01:46.242 --> 00:01:47.777
- This is what they should serve.

00:01:47.777 --> 00:01:48.610
- Let's try the last one.

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:51.205
These are edamame flavored
and I really like edamame.

00:01:51.205 --> 00:01:52.270
- These are cute!

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:53.416
These are like marshmallows.

00:01:53.416 --> 00:01:56.725
- These are really cute,
they look like Lucky Charms.

00:01:56.725 --> 00:01:57.748
- Whoa.

00:01:57.748 --> 00:01:59.911
(Steven makes confused noise)

00:01:59.911 --> 00:02:02.200
It tastes like very, very salty edamame.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:03.915
I like the edamame the best.

00:02:03.915 --> 00:02:05.961
The flavor seems a little bit more mild.

00:02:05.961 --> 00:02:08.711
[Steven sounds out Japanese word]

00:02:13.401 --> 00:02:14.923
That's a doozy.

00:02:14.923 --> 00:02:16.686
Japanese drunk snacks seem pretty buttery.

00:02:16.686 --> 00:02:17.706
- This is like Outback Steakhouse bread.

00:02:17.706 --> 00:02:19.401
Yo, they're really cute faces though.

00:02:19.401 --> 00:02:21.310
- [Jen] Yeah, they look really scared.

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:22.572
(both crunching)

00:02:22.572 --> 00:02:23.838
No, I don't like that.

00:02:23.838 --> 00:02:26.292
It kinda tastes like
wasabi that's gone bad.

00:02:26.292 --> 00:02:28.338
- Maybe they're growing
different avocados in Japan.

00:02:28.338 --> 00:02:29.862
Maybe we're doing it wrong.

00:02:29.862 --> 00:02:31.338
- Maybe avocados are
supposed to taste like that.

00:02:31.338 --> 00:02:32.171
In which case...

00:02:32.171 --> 00:02:33.522
- Good job?

00:02:33.522 --> 00:02:37.598
Oh, wow. (makes silly sound)

00:02:37.598 --> 00:02:38.431
So strong!

00:02:39.371 --> 00:02:40.204
- Fuck.

00:02:40.204 --> 00:02:41.607
- Would you eat this if you were drunk?

00:02:41.607 --> 00:02:43.265
- I mean, if I were
drunk I'd eat anything.

00:02:43.265 --> 00:02:44.299
(Steven chuckles)

00:02:44.299 --> 00:02:45.534
I would probably eat cardboard.

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:46.627
Cheese.
- It.

00:02:46.627 --> 00:02:48.182
(both crunching)

00:02:48.182 --> 00:02:50.772
- What I like about it is you
can clearly taste the cheddar

00:02:50.772 --> 00:02:51.605
and then it's very buttery.

00:02:51.605 --> 00:02:54.242
- This is like a slightly
more intense Cheez-It.

00:02:54.242 --> 00:02:55.319
- [Steven] Heck yes!

00:02:55.319 --> 00:02:56.263
See, this is what I'm talking about.

00:02:56.263 --> 00:02:57.121
- [Jen] This is good.

00:02:57.121 --> 00:02:58.346
I ate so much black sesame-flavored,

00:02:58.346 --> 00:03:00.589
so this I'm actually really excited about.

00:03:00.589 --> 00:03:01.980
- Oh yeah.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.276
That's like a drug to me.

00:03:04.276 --> 00:03:05.414
- Hit me.

00:03:05.414 --> 00:03:06.884
- Here.

00:03:06.884 --> 00:03:08.396
- That smells awesome.

00:03:08.396 --> 00:03:09.744
(Steven moans)

00:03:09.744 --> 00:03:10.577
- That's heavenly.

00:03:10.577 --> 00:03:12.260
- Let's eat it.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:13.399
(both crunching)

00:03:13.399 --> 00:03:14.419
Yeah, that's really good.

00:03:14.419 --> 00:03:18.180
- It almost has seaweed vibes,
just the mildness of it.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:19.680
"Gomaaza," you go.

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:21.829
"Maaza."

00:03:21.829 --> 00:03:23.004
I want to give somebody this set

00:03:23.004 --> 00:03:25.578
just because it looks cool
and it's fun for a party.

00:03:25.578 --> 00:03:27.295
- I mean, the thing is if
you were having a party,

00:03:27.295 --> 00:03:30.157
this is such a convenient
way to serve snacks.

00:03:30.157 --> 00:03:32.965
Just pop this down on the table,

00:03:32.965 --> 00:03:34.361
pop it open,

00:03:34.361 --> 00:03:36.311
and then everyone can just grab
something on their way out.

00:03:36.311 --> 00:03:40.037
And if there's one thing that
drunk people love, it's fun.

00:03:40.037 --> 00:03:41.776
- And games.
- Oh yeah.

00:03:41.776 --> 00:03:42.609
- Fun and games.

00:03:42.609 --> 00:03:45.240
- And toys, this seems
just like a big toy.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:46.427
- Oh yeah.

00:03:46.427 --> 00:03:49.127
- [Jen] Bye, don't tell anyone.

00:03:49.127 --> 00:03:50.269
(mellow, jazzy music)

00:03:50.269 --> 00:03:52.475
(cup clattering)

00:03:52.475 --> 00:03:55.086
- [Steven] Okay. (laughs)

00:03:55.086 --> 00:03:56.065
Wanna play beer pong?

00:03:56.065 --> 00:03:57.232
- [Jen] Yeah.

